  "content": "One killed in motorcycle accident in Kapan\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 12, 2025\n0\nComments\nImage for representation only\nKathmandu, October 12\nA 25-year-old man died this morning following a motorcycle accident in Kapan.\nAccording to Kathmandu Valley Traffic Police Office spokesperson and SP Naresh Raj Subedi, the deceased has been identified as Pasang Mingma Sherpa, originally from Solukhumbu and currently residing in Kapan.\n“The motorcycle (Ba 81 Pa 735) heading from Paiyutar to Gokarneshwar hit an electric pole near Paiyutar Water Factory last night, leaving Sherpa critically injured,” said Subedi. “He died during treatment at Kathmandu Medical College this morning.”\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nnepali cricket\nflood\nSushila Karki\ninsurance\nICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\nKapan\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nIndra Senchury and his tale of becoming a squatter\n3 years ago\nMan found dead in Kathmandu’s Dhobikhola\n3 years ago\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nSociety\nFear among Raute community after drunk intruders enter settlement; security demanded\n1 hour ago\nCricket\nNepal to face UAE in Super Six clash of ICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\n1 hour ago\nOpinion\nThe rise of Nepal’s first woman Prime Minister\n5 hours ago\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n2 days ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n2 days ago",
